Assistance Module

Developer Description and Data Structure

Purpose. The Assistance Module will record, monitor, summarize, and geographically display all assistance
provided in each barangay. Every assistance record must be linked to a barangay so the dashboard can
automatically compute the number of assistance transactions, total amount of assistance, and total beneficiaries
per barangay.

1. Staff Data Entry
When staff clicks Add Assistance, the system should require the following fields:
Field Description
Barangay Select the barangay where the assistance was

provided.

Type of Assistance Financial, Burial, Tent, Item Donation, or Others.
Assistance Given Specific description or name of the assistance

provided.

Date Date when the assistance was provided.
Amount Peso value or cost of the assistance.
Number of Beneficiaries Number of people who benefited from the assistance.
For Type of Assistance = Others, the system should allow staff to enter a custom description.

2. Automatic Barangay Summary
The system must automatically consolidate all assistance records for each barangay. Staff should not manually
compute the summary totals.
 Number of Assistance per Barangay - total count of assistance records encoded for that barangay.
 Amount of Assistance per Barangay - total peso value of all assistance provided in that barangay.
 Number of Beneficiaries per Barangay - total number of beneficiaries recorded across all assistance entries in
that barangay.

3. Example Barangay Summary
When a user clicks a barangay on the map, the system may display:
Number of Assistance 85
Total Amount of Assistance PHP 425,000
Number of Beneficiaries 312

4. Breakdown by Assistance Type
The barangay summary should also allow a breakdown by assistance type so the user can see what kind of
assistance was provided and its corresponding totals.
Type No. of Assistance Total Amount Beneficiaries
Financial 35 PHP 250,000 35
Burial 12 PHP 120,000 12
Tent 8 PHP 20,000 320
Item Donation 25 PHP 30,000 180

Others 5 PHP 5,000 20

5. Map Visualization
The Assistance map should visualize the volume or value of assistance per barangay. A user-selectable map
metric is recommended:
 Number of Assistance
 Amount of Assistance
 Number of Beneficiaries
When a metric is selected, the map should visually distinguish barangays according to their totals. Clicking a
barangay should open its summary and detailed assistance records.

6. Dashboard Filters
Recommended filters:
 Barangay / All Barangays
 Date Range
 Type of Assistance

7. Detailed Barangay Records
Date Type Assistance Given Amount Beneficiaries
Nov. 5 Financial Medical Assistance PHP 5,000 1
Nov. 8 Burial Burial Assistance PHP 10,000 1
Nov. 12 Item Donation Food Packs PHP 25,000 100

8. Core Data Logic
Barangay -> Type of Assistance -> Assistance Given -> Date -> Amount -> Number of Beneficiaries
The system will then automatically generate the following per barangay:
Number of Assistance + Total Amount of Assistance + Total Beneficiaries + Breakdown by Assistance Type

9. Reporting Capability
The same data structure should support future reports such as monthly or yearly assistance totals, assistance by
barangay, assistance by type, total beneficiaries reached, and comparisons between barangays or time periods.

